note Hop Linux file-list foundation. SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note No timer or scan runs until explicitly requested. Symlink directories are never traversed.
note File format HOPFIND1:64-byte header, then NUL-terminated absolute pathname byte strings.
note CLI JSON follows RFC8259 section7 and UTF-8 validation RFC3629 sections3/4.
note Invalid filesystem UTF-8 bytes use the reversible surrogateescape convention U+DC80..U+DCFF;
note agents must retain these escapes when round-tripping such names. Ordinary Unicode is encoded normally.
note Header0..7 magic; u64 little-endian at8 record count,16 partial-warning count,24 body bytes,
note 32 attempted-directory count;40..63 reserved zero. A newline is an ordinary pathname byte.
note Linux AArch64 stat and fcntl layouts are those of installed kernel UAPI headers.
note Directory flags O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY=49152 calc:a636669bf8335bbaf4882cbbea217a1bbb71e5037a035961710684bb41f1597c.
note Temp flags O_NOFOLLOW|O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_WRONLY=32961 calc:a20ca9614e5701d380af7d625ecc52fc9d081fc5f1c2dbce397542e1bb81313a.
note Lock flags O_NOFOLLOW|O_CREAT|O_NONBLOCK|O_RDWR=34882 calc:55d3315f96faa89f2851ea6d22b07a20adda0081bf621917b0eca71661a94ceb.
note Fixed4096 pathname buffers reflect the Linux pathname syscall boundary; directories and records grow.
note All cache operations occur relative to an open cache directory, then the original working directory is restored.
note This avoids imposing the compiler's4096-byte packed-rename boundary on a pair of long absolute paths.
